<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Tran dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">1225 CE – 1400 CE · capital Thang Long</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Vietnamese dynasty that defeated three Mongol invasions in the 13th century under the generalship of Tran Hung Dao.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Tran clan, coastal landowners from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nam-dinh">Nam Dinh</a>, gained control of the late <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ly-dynasty">Ly dynasty</a> court. In 1225 Tran Thu Do arranged the marriage of the child empress <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ly-chieu-hoang">Ly Chieu Hoang</a> to his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tran-thai-tong">Tran Canh</a>, who became emperor Tran Thai Tong, and the Tran ruled Dai Viet from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thang-long">Thang Long</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Tran rulers kept power in the family through intermarriage and a system of senior emperors who abdicated to guide their sons. Princes held large estates worked by bondsmen. The dynasty expanded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-river-asia">Red River</a> dikes, compiled the first national history, and promoted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/truc-lam-zen">Truc Lam Zen</a> school founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tran-nhan-tong">Tran Nhan Tong</a>. Writing in chu nom developed.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ly-dynasty">Dai Viet</a> repelled Mongol invasions in 1258, 1285 and 1287 to 1288, the last ending at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bach-dang-river">Bach Dang</a>. The 14th century brought wars with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/champa">Champa</a> and weak rulers, and in 1400 the minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-quy-ly">Ho Quy Ly</a> deposed the last Tran emperor, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ho-dynasty">Ho dynasty</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/tran-dynasty.jpg" alt="Tran dynasty" width="320" height="314"><figcaption>Image: Doãn Hiệu · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:VietNam(1226-1400).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1225 CE – 1400 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Thang Long</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tran Thai Tong, Tran Nhan Tong</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism, Confucianism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Vietnamese, Classical Chinese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/vietnam">Vietnam</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dai Viet, Nhà Trần</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1312&amp;focus=tran-dynasty" aria-label="Tran dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7526 1400 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tran dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7846 1656L7846 1656M7846 1656L7901 1174M7846 1656L7867 1005M7846 1656L7643 1242M7846 1656L7861 1672"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7846 1656h0M7901 1174h0M7867 1005h0M7643 1242h0M7861 1672h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7846 1656h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7846 1656h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1312&amp;focus=tran-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
